Each build round found one more syntactic route past the census: binding forms (r1), alias chains of extracted functions (r2), Date.prototype.constructor (r3). An untyped syntactic scan is not complete against code written to evade it, so revision 2 bounds the census's input domain to the forms a builder writes by mistake.

## Findings
1. advisory — the census's input domain is now the forms a builder writes by mistake: direct calls on fs bindings and Date, with any alias, destructure, store, pass, return or export of them refused by rule (already built, rounds 1-3); the Intent and behaviour 6 no longer claim "every" access in any form; default 8 — check: packages/cli/src/containment.test.ts (W-163-b6 fixture matrix)
2. advisory — one fail-closed Date member allowlist: on Date or globalThis.Date only the direct calls Date.parse(…) (a C site), Date.UTC(…) and Date.now(), plus new Date(…), Date(…), instanceof, typeof and type positions; any other member access (Date.prototype, Date.length, an uncalled Date.now) is an out-of-domain finding; no non-test source at 26fe11b uses one, so no pin is added — check: packages/cli/src/containment.test.ts (rows date-prototype, date-prototype-constructor-parse, date-prototype-constructor-new, date-global-prototype, date-other-member, date-now-uncalled; ok-control and direct stay as they are)
3. advisory — reaching fs or Date by reflection or the prototype chain (instance .constructor, Object.getPrototypeOf, Reflect, eval, new Function, globalThis[expr]) is out of scope with the threat-model reason "Mistakes, not adversaries"; no existing rule refuses eval or new Function (eslint.config.mjs enables neither no-eval nor no-new-func, and no check rule names them), none appears in the source set, and none is invented here — check: none: out of the census's domain by the threat model, stated in Out of scope
4. advisory — behaviour 6's genuine red extends to the allowlist rows: at 26fe11b the row "the scan refuses the date-prototype-constructor-parse form" fails, since memberKind gives Date.prototype no kind and nsUseSeen accepts any member access on Date — check: packages/cli/src/containment.test.ts (W-163-b6)

